  <running_head>Castigatio Paral.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">tura. 2. quòd remissâ culpâ remaneat</l>
    <l n="2">adhuc pœna solvenda, pro qua homi-</l>
    <l n="3">nes Deo satisfacere teneantur. Quasi</l>
    <l n="4">homo pœna dignus sit, licèt non sit</l>
    <l n="5">culpabilis.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Atquè hæc omnia quia vetustati, ve-</l>
    <l n="7">ritati, sacræ scripturæ, &amp; imprimis san-</l>
    <l n="8">ctissimæ &amp; sufficientissimæ satisfactio-</l>
    <l n="9">ni Christi contrariantur, dicimus, sen-</l>
    <l n="10">tentiam de satisfactionibus hodiernis</l>
    <l n="11">Romanis impiam &amp; blasphemam</l>
    <l n="12">esse.</l>
    <l n="13" type="heading" level="2" para="true">III. Bonis operibus, ex divina gratia &amp;</l>
    <l n="14" type="heading" level="2">meritorum Christi virtute profectis, vitam</l>
    <l n="15" type="heading" level="2">æternam velle mereri, esse impium.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Per bona opera, ex virtute divinæ</l>
    <l n="17">gratiæ, merito Christi impetratæ, fide-</l>
    <l n="18">les ad vitam æternam pervenire, &amp;</l>
    <l n="19">absque his neminem eò pertingere</l>
    <l n="20">posse fatemur; quòd autem propterea</l>
    <l n="21">vitam æternam mereantur, negamus.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Nam 1. Scriptura sacra ne unicum</l>
    <l n="23">locum</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The head of the page is set in roman with small capitals; the heading III is set in italic and is treated as a level 2 heading. The last line is continued on the next page.</notes>
</page>
